  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Stars X and Y have the same surface temperature. Star X has a radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> and is a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span> from Earth. The distance of star Y from Earth is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{d}{2}\"></span>. The apparent brightness of Y is double that of X.</p>\n<p>What is the radius of star Y?<br/><br/></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}R\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2R\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
